Attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project EXTENDS, and is designed to run alongside, Protocol SIFT —
an AI-driven DFIR configuration bundle for the SANS SIFT Workstation,
authored by Rob Lee and published by SANS / teamdfir
(github.com/teamdfir/protocol-sift). Protocol
SIFT is a separate work under its own license; this project does not
redistribute it. See docs/protocol-sift-integration.md for the integration
analysis.

This project is built for use on the SANS SIFT Workstation and drives the
Neo4j graph database (Neo4j 5.x Community Edition, a separate work under its
own license).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evidence dataset
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The forensic graph distributed/described with this project is derived from
the publicly published SANS FOR508 lab scenario ("Stark Research Labs" /
SHIELDBASE). All host names, account names, IP addresses, and indicators in
the graph and in the documentation are artifacts of that published training
scenario — not real persons or infrastructure. See docs/evidence-dataset.md.
